**Findings**

- **P1**: `TraceLog::event()` is not exception-contained. It copies JSON and calls `dump()` before the mutex, and callers build JSON initializer lists before entering it. A throw can escape guarded error handlers or mask cancellation paths, e.g. queue cancel at [metal_server.cpp:682](/Users/macthedan/projects/q27/src/metal/metal_server.cpp:682), prefill cancel at [metal_server.cpp:829](/Users/macthedan/projects/q27/src/metal/metal_server.cpp:829), and catch chains at [metal_server.cpp:1253](/Users/macthedan/projects/q27/src/metal/metal_server.cpp:1253) / [metal_server.cpp:1290](/Users/macthedan/projects/q27/src/metal/metal_server.cpp:1290). The sink itself is at [metal_server.cpp:297](/Users/macthedan/projects/q27/src/metal/metal_server.cpp:297). This violates “trace cannot throw through handlers/run cancellation.”

- **P2**: trace-off is not fully side-effect-free. Most importantly, `/v1/completions` has an unguarded request trace at [metal_server.cpp:1336](/Users/macthedan/projects/q27/src/metal/metal_server.cpp:1336), including `body.value("prompt","")` and `trace_text(...)` at [metal_server.cpp:1338](/Users/macthedan/projects/q27/src/metal/metal_server.cpp:1338). That is the expensive request path the `enabled()` guard was supposed to cover.

- **P2**: mid-request cancellation tracing is incomplete/misclassified. Generation-side disconnects set `client_gone` in `deliver()` at [metal_server.cpp:911](/Users/macthedan/projects/q27/src/metal/metal_server.cpp:911), return `Finish::Cancelled` at [metal_server.cpp:1090](/Users/macthedan/projects/q27/src/metal/metal_server.cpp:1090), then are reported through normal outcome paths, not `{"kind":"cancel","phase":"midrequest"}`. The guarded `midrequest` events at [metal_server.cpp:1253](/Users/macthedan/projects/q27/src/metal/metal_server.cpp:1253) and [metal_server.cpp:1290](/Users/macthedan/projects/q27/src/metal/metal_server.cpp:1290) only catch thrown `ClientGone`, which is queue/prefill in this code, and they do not include the request id.

- **P2**: `tms` monotonicity is not guaranteed in file order. `tms` is captured before acquiring the trace mutex at [metal_server.cpp:299](/Users/macthedan/projects/q27/src/metal/metal_server.cpp:299), while write ordering is determined after locking at [metal_server.cpp:304](/Users/macthedan/projects/q27/src/metal/metal_server.cpp:304). Two worker threads can therefore write a later `tms` line before an earlier one. The gate asserts monotonic file order at [trace_gate.sh:41](/Users/macthedan/projects/q27/tools/trace_gate.sh:41).

- **P2**: `--trace -` is not a clean JSONL stream. `open("-")` points tracing at `stderr` at [metal_server.cpp:292](/Users/macthedan/projects/q27/src/metal/metal_server.cpp:292), but normal `fprintf(stderr, ...)` logging still writes there, including tool fallback logs such as [metal_server.cpp:1460](/Users/macthedan/projects/q27/src/metal/metal_server.cpp:1460). That breaks the “TraceLog::event is the only writer” property for the `-` mode.

- **P3**: three ctx-limit preflight error events omit the known request id: completions [metal_server.cpp:1330](/Users/macthedan/projects/q27/src/metal/metal_server.cpp:1330), chat [metal_server.cpp:1414](/Users/macthedan/projects/q27/src/metal/metal_server.cpp:1414), and messages [metal_server.cpp:1614](/Users/macthedan/projects/q27/src/metal/metal_server.cpp:1614). Responses includes it at [metal_server.cpp:1923](/Users/macthedan/projects/q27/src/metal/metal_server.cpp:1923). The `run()` threading itself looks correct for completions/chat/messages/responses.

- **P3**: prefix tier can be mislabeled as disk when memory and disk have equal hit length. Disk is only loaded when `disk_len > hit` at [metal_server.cpp:747](/Users/macthedan/projects/q27/src/metal/metal_server.cpp:747), but the event labels `disk` when `disk_ok && hit == disk_len` at [metal_server.cpp:766](/Users/macthedan/projects/q27/src/metal/metal_server.cpp:766).

**Verified**

Tool recovery trace calls are present beside each `[tool-fallback]` fprintf I found. Eviction counters count successful removes under `DiskSnapshotStore::m_` at [metal_server.cpp:257](/Users/macthedan/projects/q27/src/metal/metal_server.cpp:257); in-progress saves write `.tmp` then rename, so the evict scan does not see partial `.q27snap` files. `count_tokens` correctly has no outcome in the gate because it is CPU-only and never calls `run()`; the gate excludes it from expected outcomes at [trace_gate.sh:50](/Users/macthedan/projects/q27/tools/trace_gate.sh:50).
